Package: truedca
Title: Decision Curve Analysis for Outcomes Recorded with Error
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Marwan", "Alqumbaey", email = "marwanalqumbaey@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-8688-9556")),
    person("Yousef M.", "Nasher", email = "yousefnasher76@gmail.com",
           role = "aut", comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-3704-3149")))
Description: Decision curves for clinical prediction models when the outcome
    used for evaluation is recorded with error, as with diagnosis codes or
    text-mined labels. Provides observed and corrected net benefit, the
    thresholds at which a decision curve cannot be informative, sharp bounds
    and tipping points when error rates are only partly known, estimation from
    two-phase chart review designs with simultaneous confidence bands,
    optimal chart review sampling probabilities and their expected gain, and
    probabilistic bias analysis when no chart review is possible.
